ns and  took inspiration from multiple locations  around europe to create the capital  using animation they referenced a few  different styles of architecture in  order to create a place that looked  incredibly intimidating but also a  little familiar  all of the hunger games movies feature  some seriously  huge crowd scenes and the extravagant  opening ceremony has got to be one of  the most impressive  inspired by the ancient chariot races  and gladiator battles of ancient rome  the tributes are cheered on by thousands  of capital citizens sitting in the  stands  except almost none of those citizens  were actually there  they were all added in later by  animators which is a whole lot cheaper  and  far easier than hiring placing and  costuming  thousands of background actors so  clearly  are able to reflect the character of  each district  everyone who's seen the hunger games  might be pretty glad to find out that  the giant and terrifying mutts that  chased peta and katniss through the  woods  were actually totally animated cgi  artists used the descriptions from the  books to painstakingly bring the  creatures to life  and they did an amazing job the finished  mutts look a little bit like steroid  using rottweilers  whose faces have been smushed with a  frying pan  and are not something we want to run  into in real life there was no debate  about the fact that whoever scored the  role of katniss would have to train hard  to believably pull off some of the  incredible archery that the character's  capable of  and jennifer lawrence did just that she  trained with a five-time  olympic archer for 15 hours in order to  nail the sport  and most archery experts agree but she  nailed it  but when it came to actually shooting  arrows on camera  the production actually decided it would  be a lot safer to animate  all of her arrows for the safety of  everyone on set  she's not even afraid of us one of the  most heartbreaking moments from the  second hunger games movie  catching fire was the scene in which  peta and katniss pay a visit to district  11.  if you know the franchise you knew that  district 11 was rue's district  so this particular visit was devastating  for katniss  what you might not have realized about  the relatively simple scene  is that much of it was animated from the  screens playing images of roo's face  to the size of the crowd and the  location itself  we like to donate one month of our  winnings to the families of the tributes  every year for the rest of our lives as  katniss and peeta continue their  victor's tour of all the districts  it becomes clear that the unrest they  sparked during the games is spreading  across pan  am in one instance the gathered crowd  becomes upset by their lack of action  against the capital  and rushed the stage before katniss and  peeta are rushed off to safety  even though this scene seems like it  would be easy enough to do with a crowd  of real people  the digital effects artists actually  used a small group  and multiplied it over and over in order  to make the crowd even bigger  katniss's home district district 12 is  one of the poorest in  all of pan am 12 is also responsible for  providing  coal to the capital so it's all centered  around huge mines that most citizens  work in  day in and day out while there are  plenty of mining towns throughout the  u.s  what you see in the film is you guessed  it cgi  rather than building giant cranes and  oil rigs they simply  shot in front of a blue screen and added  them in afterwards  the tributes from district 12.  one of the most action-packed sequences  from mockingjay part 2  is definitely the chase scene inside the  berlin metro station between the capitol  peacekeepers and katniss  and the star squad during this scene we  get to see some  seriously cool cgi moments one of these  moments occurs when a member of the star  squad  runs underneath a circular beam of light  and is  shattered into a million pieces it is a  very sad moment for the rebels  but an amazing piece of animation the  beams of exploding light weren't the  only impressive effects to use during  that sequence either  as this next one demonstrates just how  much cgi can enhance a movie in ways  that practical effects just  can't quite pull off during the same  metro fight just as we thought the  rebels were almost on their way to  safety the entire floor starts exploding  underneath their feet  and all they can do is try and outrun it  before it swallows them  it was a huge task bringing these  beloved books to life on the big screen  there were some moments that the  filmmakers knew the fans were going to  be waiting for  and katniss's flaming dress during the  opening ceremony was  definitely one of them and it didn't  disappoint  but fortunately for jennifer lawrence  they didn't actually light her on fire  for the sake of the movie  all of the flames you see erupting from  her stunning red dress were actually cgi  that was something that was something  thank you for that  there are many things in the hunger  games that we are  very glad don't actually exist in real  life  and on the top of that list are the  tracker jackers  designed to look like giant genetically  modified hornets  these terrifying creatures look way too  real during the scene when katniss  knocks one of their nests out of a tree  after being chased up by an  all-too-eager group of hunger games  tributes  when we first visit district 13 one of  the most impressive parts of it  is their giant underground weapons  facility  almost the entire thing was animated  even though they did build some  very realistic looking nuclear weapons  to go inside it  because it would be almost impossible to  find a location  that was as big as district 13 needed to  be  it was a whole lot easier to shoot it on  a blue screen and bring it up to scale  using cgi  quick introductions catas these people  come a long way  while the hunger games movies had a  pretty huge budget  it wasn't quite enough to cover the  building of a futuristic military-level  hovercraft  so the very impressive one that we see  rise up out of the floor and mockingjay  part 1  was in fact animated  yeah that's a mockingjay honestly the  effects in the hunger games are so  amazing that we might never have known  that none of it was real  what about you let us know what you  thought about this video in the comments  and don't forget to hit subscribe to  keep up with  all of our latest videos

